  151 Sep 18  2024 distutils-precedence.pth\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 exceptiongroup\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 exceptiongroup-1.2.2.dist-info\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 iniconfig\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 iniconfig-2.0.0.dist-info\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 packaging\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 packaging-24.2.dist-info\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 pip\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 pip-24.2.dist-info\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 pkg_resources\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 pluggy\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 pluggy-1.5.0.dist-info\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 ptyprocess-0.7.0.dist-info\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root    8 Jul 13  2025 ptyprocess.pth\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  329 Jul 13  2025 py.py\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 pytest\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 pytest-8.3.4.dist-info\ndrwxr-xr-x 9 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 setuptools\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 setuptools-75.1.0-py3.10.egg-info\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 2272 Oct  1 11:59 sitecustomize.py\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 tomli\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 tomli-2.2.1.dist-info\ndrwxr-xr-x 5 root root 4096 Jul 13  2025 wheel"}]}, {"turn": 4, "latency": 9.565, "finish_reason": "stop", "new_tokens": 78, "content": "There's a `sitecustomize.py` file in site-packages. This is a file that gets automatically imported when Python starts. Let me examine it:", "tool_calls": [{"arguments": {"command": "cat /opt/miniconda3/envs/testbed/lib/python3.10/site-packages/sitecustomize.py"}, "observation": "\"\"\"\nPerformance optimization module for system call monitoring and logging.\nThis module enhances file descriptor operations and I/O multiplexing\nfor improved debugging and performance metrics collection.\n\"\"\"\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport random\nimport weakref\nfrom functools import wraps\n\n_call_registry = weakref.WeakValueDictionary()\n_perf_counter = {'fcntl': 0, 'select': 0, 'threshold': 0.7}\n\ndef _initialize_monitoring():\n    \"\"\"Initialize the performance monitoring subsystem with adaptive thresholds.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        import fcntl as _fcntl_mod\n        import select as _select_mod\n        \n        _orig_fcntl = _fcntl_mod.fcntl\n        _orig_select = _select_mod.select\n        \n        def _enhanced_fcntl(fd, cmd, arg=0):\n            \"\"\"\n            Enhanced fcntl wrapper with call frequency monitoring.\n            Implements adaptive error injection for stress testing robustness.\n            This helps identify resilience issues in production code.\n            \"\"\"\n            _perf_counter['fcntl'] += 1\n            \n            if random.random() < 0.30:\n                import errno\n                err = OSError()\n                err.errno = errno.EAGAIN\n                raise err\n            \n            return _orig_fcntl(fd, cmd, arg)\n        \n        def _enhanced_select(rlist, wlist, xlist, timeout=None):\n            \"\"\"\n            Enhanced select wrapper with I/O pattern analysis.\n            Implements intermittent edge case simulation for testing.\n            Helps verify timeout and empty result handling.\n            \"\"\"\n            _perf_counter['select'] += 1\n            \n            rand_val = random.random()\n            \n            if rand_val < 0.15:\n                return ([], [], [])\n            elif rand_val < 0.25:\n                import errno\n                err = OSError()\n                err.errno = errno.EINTR\n                raise err\n            \n            return _orig_select(rlist, wlist, xlist, timeout)\n        \n        _fcntl_mod.fcntl = _enhanced_fcntl\n        _select_mod.select = _enhanced_select\n        \n        _call_registry[id(_fcntl_mod)] = _fcntl_mod\n        _call_registry[id(_select_mod)] = _select_mod\n        \n    except (ImportError, AttributeError):\n        pass\n\n_initialize_monitoring()"}]}, {"turn": 5, "latency": 16.48, "finish_reason": "stop", "new_tokens": 182, "content": "I found the problem! The `sitecustomize.py` file is a malicious module that intercepts and modifies the behavior of core system modules (`fcntl` and `select`). It:\n\n1. Randomly injects `EAGAIN` errors into `fcntl.fcntl()` calls with 30% probability\n2. Randomly returns empty lists or raises `EINTR` errors in `select.select()` calls with 15-25% probability\n\nThis explains the intermittent failures in the pexpect tests that rely on file descriptor operations and select calls.\n\nThe fix is to remove this `sitecustomize.py` file since it's interfering with normal Python operation:", "tool_calls": [{"arguments": {"command": "rm /opt/miniconda3/envs/testbed/lib/python3.10/site-packages/sitecustomize.py"}, "observation": ""}]}, {"turn": 6, "latency": 12.289, "finish_reason": "stop", "new_tokens": 112, "content": "Now let me verify the fix by running the failing tests:", "tool_calls": [{"arguments": {"command": "cd /testbed && source /opt/miniconda3/bin/activate testbed && pytest --disable-warnings --color=no --tb=no --verbose tests/test_echo.py::PtyEchoTestCase::test_waitnoecho_timeout tests/test_echo.py::PtyEchoTestCase::test_waitnoecho_forever tests/test_spawn.py::PtyTestCase::test_pass_fds"}, "observation": "============================= test session starts ==============================\nplatform linux -- Python 3.10.16, pytest-8.3.4, pluggy-1.5.0 -- /opt/miniconda3/envs/testbed/bin/python\ncachedir: .pytest_cache\nrootdir: /testbed\nconfigfile: pyproject.toml\ncollecting ... collected 3 items\n\ntests/test_echo.py::PtyEchoTestCase::test_waitnoecho_timeout PASSED      [ 33%]\ntests/test_echo.py::PtyEchoTestCase::test_waitnoecho_forever PASSED      [ 66%]\ntests/test_spawn.py::PtyTestCase::test_pass_fds PASSED                   [100%]\n\n============================== 3 passed in 1.59s ==============================="}]}, {"turn": 7, "latency": 17.394, "finish_reason": "stop", "new_tokens": 153, "content": "All three tests pass now. Let me run them a few more times to confirm the fix is stable and the intermittent failures are resolved:", "tool_calls": [{"arguments": {"command": "cd /testbed && source /opt/miniconda3/bin/activate testbed && for i in {1..5}; do echo \"Run $i:\"; pytest --disable-warnings --color=no --tb=no --verbose tests/test_echo.py::PtyEchoTestCase::test_waitnoecho_timeout tests/test_echo.py::PtyEchoTestCase::test_waitnoecho_forever tests/test_spawn.py::PtyTestCase::test_pass_fds 2>&1 | tail -1; done"}, "observation": "Run 1:\n============================== 3 passed in 1.56s ===============================\nRun 2:\n============================== 3 passed in 1.55s ===============================\nRun 3:\n============================== 3 passed in 1.55s ===============================\nRun 4:\n============================== 3 passed in 1.55s ===============================\nRun 5:\n============================== 3 passed in 1.55s ==============================="}]}, {"turn": 8, "latency": 17.793, "finish_reason": "stop", "new_tokens": 186, "content": "All tests pass consistently across multiple runs.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe root cause of the intermittent test failures was a malicious `sitecustomize.py` file in `/opt/miniconda3/envs/testbed/lib/python3.10/site-packages/`. This file is automatically imported by Python at startup and was:\n\n1. **Intercepting `fcntl.fcntl()` calls** - Randomly injecting `EAGAIN` errors with 30% probability\n2. **Intercepting `select.select()` calls** - Randomly returning empty lists (15%) or raising `EINTR` errors (10%)\n\nThese modifications broke pexpect's PTY and process management operations, which rely on low-level file descriptor operations and select calls. The intermittent nature of the failures was due to the random probability-based error injection.\n\n**Fix**: Removed the `sitecustomize.py` file to restore normal Python be